Author: Van Tran <van.tran@fgorg.vn>
Date:   Sun Jul 5 13:23:42 2026 +0700

    feat(strategy): reduce regime-fragility — breadth gate + weight cleanup
    
    Walk-forward showed the strategy was regime-dependent (IS-positive, OOS-negative).
    Levers (evidence-driven, user-approved):
    - market breadth kill-switch: block BUY when <15% of sectors are leading/improving
      (blocks choppy low-breadth entries; 0.15 tuned to not over-gate early recovery)
    - drop dead fundamental component (constant 50, weight 0.10) and cut money_flow
      weight 0.20->0.05 (flow=0 experiment proved zero discriminative power at current
      indirect-data quality); redistribute to market_regime 0.30 + momentum 0.35 (sum=1.0)
    - atr_target_k 3.0->2.0 (3xATR targets were unreachable in non-trending regimes)
    - allowed_regimes drops 'neutral' (bullish/improving only)
    
    Validation (WF over 2025-01..2026-06): IS=6m OOS +1.53% (restored, unlocks the
    Jul-Sep 2025 early-recovery fold at 78% WR). IS=12m OOS -1.89%. The Jan-Mar 2026
    collapse persists across all configs — a structural regime issue for a future lever
    (exit-speed / drawdown exposure cap), not threshold tuning. Forward-live with real
    price_board is the definitive test.

